# Runtime scratch. The harness runs its containers as root and writes into
# these bind mounts, so after a run they are ROOT-OWNED and sometimes
# unreadable. They must never enter the repo-root Docker build context (they
# did, and the build died with "error from sender: permission denied" every
# night from 2026-10-17 to 2026-10-27 — see .dockerignore and rule 62).
work/
data/
freeze-work/

# Generated per run by run.sh (mode 600). Never committed: even a harness
# password is a credential, and the reset is free.
config/password

# A root-owned scratch dir that cannot be deleted without sudo is moved aside
# with this suffix instead of being force-removed. The next run recreates the
# real one, so these are pure litter and safe to delete once permissions allow.
*.stale-root-*/
